Rule 2 (out must be a tensor with a floating or complex dtype)
{v_3 : tensor} |= (6 ≤ dtype_(v_3)) ∧ (dtype_(v_3) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 3 (out’s shape aligns with the broadcasted shape of input and other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1)) ∧ (ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_2)) ∧ (if ndim(v_3) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : (shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)))
>>
Rule 4 (dtype coherence to avoid invalid casts: complex inputs require complex out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10) then (dtype_(v_3) = 10) else if (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9) then (dtype_(v_3) ≥ 9) else (6 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 8)
